[Music]  here we go again sony have revealed the  games playstation plus subscribers will  receive for the month of may 2022. you  can download the following games from  tuesday the 3rd of may be sure to leave  your opinion in the comments below as i  know the playstation do read them so  let's crack on on both the ps4 and ps5  is tribes of midgar it calls itself a  co-op survival action rpg which supports  10-player cooperative play we set up our  viking village and are tasked with  protecting the seed of idrisil a big  magic tree every time night falls  creatures from the underworld attack  your village this continues until  ragnarok arrives the end of the world  that tree eats souls by the way and it's  our job to bring them to it in exchange  for new abilities after creating our own  viking we can go it alone or bring in  team mates and work together while  exploring the world we'll gather  materials for crafting items such as  armor potions and even our hometown's  defenses tribes of midgard is  procedurally generated making every area  a new game a completely different  experience oh and i forgot to mention  the best thing giants at random points a  game ending giant will begin marching  towards your home if you've prepared  well enough this is your chance to  defeat a legendary foe and collect its  very rare loot and then do it all over  again the user and critic review say  this is a 7 out of 10 game so will you  try it and more importantly do you have  9 friends to play with next we have fifa  22 on both the ps5 and ps4 whether you  call it football or prefer soccer you do  you fifa received its annual update and  this year it's slower than previous  iterations to try and combat the meta of  finding the fastest players and running  forward this is down to a refined  animation system which forces each  player to use the correct body shape  before releasing the ball a patient  build up and a more considered approach  is rewarded and thanks to that the game  looks more like real life than ever  before if the core of fifa is becoming  simulation then volta is 100  the arcade version if you've ever played  fifa street you'll know the idea smaller  courts smaller teams more flair on the  ball and more aggression too there are  many games to play for quick xp farming  and a break from the more serious parts  of fifa other improvements include  creating your own team designing their  kit and crest and steering them up the  football league buying marquee players  along the way if you've played fifa  before it's definitely more fifa and  it's easily the best football game on  the market but there isn't much  competition if i'm honest what are your  thoughts on receiving a sports game in  ps plus and finally on the ps4 is curse  of the dead gods a top down action  roguelike which has impressive reviews  we journey to a temple and make our way  through its procedurally generated  levels using 10 different weapon types  each weapon and upgrade we find will  offer slightly different stats like  elemental damage health regen or other  slight buffs but this is a roguelike so  if we die we must restart the entire  game luckily there are some permanent  upgrades to unlock on good runs which  give us a step up on our next attempt  curse of the dead gods fighting  mechanics are addicting with a stamina  meter those diamonds underneath our hero  count down and therefore must be managed  and so do the curses we pick up on route  these debuffs can only be cleansed by  defeating a boss the end goal is to  complete the entire game in one single  life and that'll take you around 30  hours i'm told ign say this game is  amazing giving it 9 out of 10. will you  try it what do you think to this month i  think i'm going to jump into tribes of  midgar what are you playing please let  me know in the comments below i'm adam  you're awesome i'll see you next time  [Music]

